Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: the data model's registration traces to em's debug channel

With 0237 to 0239 em_ctrl stayed under its journal's cap (1000 lines per 30 s) through the
rooms, but not at its own start: lab-bringup restarts it for every room setup, and it then
logged each Data Elements table it registered on the bus and each YANG path it converted
for it, some 800 lines, while every agent onboarded again (rdk-emosa-1005, 6 October 2026:
1,238 lines dropped in the window of a restart). Those traces now print through
em_util_dbg_print, as 0237 does (/nvram/emCtrlDbg); a registration that fails stays on the
journal.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/ctrl/tr_181/wfa_data_model/tr_181.cpp
+++ b/src/ctrl/tr_181/wfa_data_model/tr_181.cpp
@@ -378,7 +378,7 @@
         em_printfout("bus: bus_regDataElements failed:%s\n", full_namespace);
         return RETURN_ERR;
     }
-    em_printfout("bus: bus_regDataElements success:%s", full_namespace);
+    em_util_dbg_print(EM_CTRL, "bus: bus_regDataElements success:%s", full_namespace);
 
     return RETURN_OK;
 }
@@ -1059,7 +1059,7 @@
 std::string tr_181_t::yang_to_tr181_path(const std::string& in)
 {
     std::string out = in;
-    em_printfout("Converting YANG path: %s", in.c_str());
+    em_util_dbg_print(EM_CTRL, "Converting YANG path: %s", in.c_str());
 
     for (int i = 0; g_yang_map[i].yang; ++i) {
         const std::string from = g_yang_map[i].yang;
@@ -1229,7 +1229,7 @@
     // 0) If property is deprecated, do not bother
     bool deprecated = schema_is_deprecated(propertySchema);
     if (deprecated) {
-        em_printfout("Deprecated parameter, skip");
+        em_util_dbg_print(EM_CTRL, "Deprecated parameter, skip");
         return;
     }
 
